   "html_text": "The problem of induction is closely linked to the issue of simplicity. One obvious link is between the curve-fitting problem and the inductive problem of predicting future outcomes from observed data. Less obviously, Schulte (1999) argues for a connection between induction and ontological parsimony. Schulte frames the problem of induction in information-theoretic terms: given a data-stream of observations of non-unicorns (for example), what general conclusion should be drawn? He argues for two c",
