   "shape_m": "p",
   "html_text": "With respect to question (ii), there is an important distinction to be made between two sorts of simplicity principle. Occam’s Razor may be formulated as an epistemic principle: if theory ⟦M⟧ is simpler than theory ⟦M⟧ , then it is rational (other things being equal) to believe ⟦M⟧ rather than ⟦M⟧ . Or it may be formulated as a methodological principle: if ⟦M⟧ is simpler than ⟦M⟧ then it is rational to adopt ⟦M⟧ as one’s working theory for scientific purposes. These two conceptions of Occam’s Ra",
